maria.g: Heads up — PR #4283 adds a Node SDK snippet for span sampling and the cost/latency breakdown in Console-observability docs but the dashboard link in the snippet is 404 and the sampling example might be misleading about head vs tail sampling. Can someone sanity-check before I merge? :eyes:

leah.docs: I saw that — thanks. I can review the prose. Omar can you verify the SDK call is correct? cc @omar.engineer

omar.engineer: On it. Quick note: our SDK exposes sampling as a per-route policy and the example in the PR uses `globalSampling.rate` which doesn't exist. That would mislead customers into thinking they can change it on the fly with that field.

maria.g: ugh, ok. PR author added it to hit the cost tradeoff section, but we need to be precise because customers tune this for latency vs cost.

omar.engineer: Proposed snippet (Node):

```js
// set per-route span sampling in the Redwood SDK (pseudo-example)
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference-sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

client.routes.update('chat-route', {
  tracing: {
    spanSampling: {
      mode: 'per_span', // 'per_span' | 'per_trace'  (tail sampling requires per_trace processing)
      rate: 0.02 // 2% of spans, lowers cost but increases sampling variance
    }
  }
});

// note: tail sampling requires server-side trace-collector config, not just SDK flags
```

leah.docs: Nice. Could we add a short inline sentence that tail sampling (per_trace) will capture entire traces but is heavier on CPU/memory in the collector and therefore may change cost profile? Also add a pointer to the Console dashboard we link to.

maria.g: yes. The current link in the PR points to:/docs/console/observability/dashboards/example-traces -> returns 404. The correct stable path is /console/observability/dashboards/trace-sampling-overview (internal).

leah.docs: I'll update the copy and change the link. Also can we include a tiny before/after cost example to make the tradeoff concrete? e.g.,
- Uniform sampling at 100%: high accuracy, baseline cost X
- Per-span 2%: ~0.02 * token/ingest cost for spans — roughly 30% saved on trace ingest in sample workload
- Per-trace tail sampling 10%: higher CPU on collectors, ~0.08 cost reduction but more downstream compute

omar.engineer: I can add a note in the SDK section: "SDK flags control client-side sampling decisions; full tail sampling requires collector configuration (see collector guide)". Also add the exact JSON payload used by the Console API to update sampling so it's copy-pasteable:

```json
{
  "route": "chat-route",
  "tracing": {
    "spanSampling": {
      "mode": "per_span",
      "rate": 0.02
    }
  }
}
```

maria.g: Great. Two follow-ups before merge: 1) replace broken dashboard link, 2) add a small 'implications' callout about cost/latency.

leah.docs: I'll push a tiny PR update in the branch in ~30m.

docs-bot: PR #4283 updated by leah.docs — http://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4283 (checks running)

omar.engineer: also noticed the Node snippet used `require('@redwood/sdk')` in the PR which is the older package name. Make sure we standardize on `@redwood/inference-sdk` in all new samples.

maria.g: Good catch. Add that to the PR checklist.

leah.docs: Updated the branch: fixed link, swapped package name, added collector note and a tiny cost example. Leaving one TODO about a screenshot for the dashboard (low priority).

deploy-bot: Staging docs site rebuild queued (branch: fix/span-sampling-snippet).

maria.g: Thanks all. If staging preview looks good I'll merge later today. If someone can eyeball the preview once deploy finishes that would be awesome. :thumbsup:

omar.engineer: I'll check the preview and the JSON payloads. If anything else, I'll leave small inline comments.

leah.docs: Thanks — appreciate the quick turnaround.

maria.g: merging after green.
